{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"Given that \\(2i\\) is a root of the polynomial \\(z^4 + az^3 + 5z^2 - iz - 6 = 0\\), and since the coefficients of the polynomial are real except for the coefficient of \\(z\\), the complex conjugate \\(-2i\\) must also be a root. Therefore, the polynomial can be factored as:\n\n\\[\n(z - 2i)(z + 2i)(z^2 + bz + c)\n\\]\n\nFirst, we compute the product of the factors \\(z - 2i\\) and \\(z + 2i\\):\n\n\\[\n(z - 2i)(z + 2i) = z^2 - (2i)^2 = z^2 + 4\n\\]\n\nSo the polynomial can be written as:\n\n\\[\n(z^2 + 4)(z^2 + bz + c) = z^4 + bz^3 + (c+4)z^2 + 4bz + 4c\n\\]\n\nWe know this must be equal to the original polynomial \\(z^4 + az^3 + 5z^2 - iz - 6\\). By comparing coefficients, we get:\n\n\\[\nz^4 + bz^3 + (c+4)z^2 + 4bz + 4c = z^4 + az^3 + 5z^2 - iz - 6\n\\]\n\nFrom the comparison, we have:\n\n1. \\(b = a\\)\n2. \\(c + 4 = 5 \\implies c = 1\\)\n3. \\(4b = -i \\implies 4a = -i \\implies a = -\\frac{i}{4}\\)\n4. \\(4c = -6 \\implies 4 \\cdot 1 = -6\\), which is consistent with \\(c = 1\\)\n\n","prefix_end":936,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[22043,429,17767,17,72,57758,374,264,3704,315,279,47311,17767,89,61,19,488,12376,61,18,488,220,20,89,61,17,481,22137,481,220,21,284,220,15,59,701,323,2474,279,36829,315,279,47311,525,1931,3650,369,279,35606,315,17767,89,59,701,279,6351,63280,349,1124,4080,17,72,57758,1969,1083,387,264,3704,13,15277,11,279,47311,646,387,2097,3018,438,1447,59,9640,13174,481,220,17,72,2376,89,488,220,17,72,2376,89,61,17,488,80167,488,272,340,59,2533,5338,11,582,12564,279,1985,315,279,9363,17767,89,481,220,17,72,57758,323,17767,89,488,220,17,72,59,7731,59,9640,13174,481,220,17,72,2376,89,488,220,17,72,8,284,1147,61,17,481,320,17,72,29776,17,284,1147,61,17,488,220,19,198,59,2533,4416,279,47311,646,387,5326,438,1447,59,9640,13174,61,17,488,220,19,2376,89,61,17,488,80167,488,272,8,284,1147,61,19,488